# Tracer: mixed-carrier forall conclusions projected to stored facts.
#
# Before (did not work):
# forall a R, b set:
#     a = a
#     b = b
# Former behavior: Litex verified the statement, but strict Litex-to-Lean failed
# because the source-wide forall had no FactId after runtime projected its two
# independently covered conclusions.
#
# Now (verified and compiled):
forall a R, b set:
    a = a
    b = b
# Current behavior: Litex-to-Lean emits the two runtime-stored forall projections,
# preserving `a : ℝ`, polymorphic `b : Set α`, and both stored FactIds.
#
# Boundary: the separate equalities do not unify the real carrier of `a` with
# the element carrier of `b`; the Rust regression still rejects `a = b` here.
# Evidence: target/release/litex -compact -isolated -runner -f examples/05_compiler_interop/compile_to_lean_mixed_projected_forall.lit
# Focused compiler gate: cargo test --release compile_to_lean_mixed_projected_forall -- --nocapture
# Mathlib gate: LITEX_LEAN_PROJECT=<mathlib-project> LITEX_LAKE=<lake-path> cargo test --release compile_to_lean_mixed_projected_forall_compiles_with_lean -- --ignored --nocapture
# Implementation: src/runtime/runtime_store_fact.rs,
# src/runtime/runtime_litex_to_lean_ir.rs, src/litex_to_lean_ir/mod.rs, and
# src/compile_to_lean/pipeline.rs
